 ## 2026-08-11
 
+### 1736 — macOS provider captures one complete non-secret SSH profile generation (TASK-260715-3f4lxy)
+- IMPLEMENTATION: `SSHProfileSnapshotV1` now carries the accepted complete profile, canonical endpoint, credential reference/generation, ordered host-key policy, and trust history as immutable value types. A strict deterministic JSON pass enforces UTF-8, sorted keys, canonical strings/numbers, no insignificant whitespace, duplicate rejection, depth 8, exact v1 envelope headers, recursive prohibited-field names, and exhaustive field invariants before exposing the model.
+- DECISION: The 4096-byte bound is checked over the actual binary-property-list representation of the exact three-key `providerConfiguration`, so owner and manager-contract metadata count toward the NetworkExtension envelope. The macOS adapter reads only `NETunnelProviderProtocol.providerConfiguration`; it has no App Group, Keychain, route, network, packet, or profile-write path.
+- GENERATION SAFETY: A fresh `SSHProfileRuntimeSnapshotLoader` owns one runtime start. Byte-identical rereads return the original capture; stale profile/generation expectations, same-generation field replacement, newer-generation replacement, and concurrent competing captures fail with the fixed privacy-safe `profileGenerationMismatch` error.
+- VERIFICATION: Thirteen focused Swift Testing cases pass for DNS/IDNA A-label/IPv4/IPv6 canonicalization, Unicode and malformed names, scalar bounds, required credential/trust structures, trust record invariants, JSON corruption/oversize/duplicates/depth/version transitions, prohibited fields, providerConfiguration integration, and atomic replacement. One unrelated full-suite HEV UDP association assertion failed transiently, its 12-test suite immediately passed on isolated rerun, and the complete 391-test/32-suite retry passed; no loader failure occurred.
+
 ### 1616 — Physical Mac P0 row passes; account prerequisite evidence remains blocked (TASK-260715-2ayxqn)
 - PHYSICAL RESULT: Accepted `TASK-260715-9yp8to` evidence proves provider install and PlugInKit discovery on Mac15,9 arm64/macOS 26.5, matching signed profiles and entitlements, ten launch/versioned-message/stop cycles, controlled reinstall, one manager, one provider registration, zero residual provider processes, and zero crashes.
 - GATE DISPOSITION: Overall macOS Gate P0 is BLOCKED, not a conditional pass. The accepted `TASK-260715-apc34w` readiness audit explicitly remains NOT READY because organization enrollment/active paid-through date, current DPLA or Free Apps Agreement status, and the accountable Admin/C&I&P grant were not captured. This task's fail-closed AC3 forbids inferring those missing in-scope prerequisites from successful Mac lifecycle evidence.
